{"date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Pop Culture Digest — Sunday, September 20, 2026", "link": "https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/", "pubDate": "Sun, 20 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0500", "description": "\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n\n  <tr><td style=\"background:#111111;padding:24px 18px 20px;color:#ffffff;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c9a66b;\">Sunday · catch-up send</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin-top:8px;font-weight:normal;\">Pop Culture Digest</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#d0d0d0;margin-top:8px;\">Sunday, September 20, 2026 · What’s actually dominating today</div>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:18px 18px 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#444;\">\n    Four stories owning the conversation today: Zach Cregger’s <em>Resident Evil</em> smashes the franchise open, Ed Sheeran turns a brutal week into a Philly catharsis, New Found Glory’s Chad Gilbert is mourned at 45, and Jhené Aiko finally lands her first Billboard 200 No. 1.\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 1 Resident Evil -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9a3412;font-weight:600;\">Movies</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\"><em>Resident Evil</em> opens to a franchise-record $60 million</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/resident-evil-box-office-zach-cregger-reboot-opening-weekend-record-breaking-1236867659/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/img1.jpg\" alt=\"Resident Evil 2026\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Zach Cregger’s reboot didn’t just clear the bar — it reset it. Sony estimates a $60M domestic opening (vs. a $40–50M track) and $108.3M worldwide, both franchise highs, with a Certified Fresh ~96% on Rotten Tomatoes. Austin Abrams stars as a medical courier sprinting through Raccoon City; word of mouth is carrying what last weekend’s soft <em>Practical Magic 2</em> couldn’t.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/resident-evil-box-office-zach-cregger-reboot-opening-weekend-record-breaking-1236867659/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety box office&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XKOVrTqXncw\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/fav_youtube.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Trailer&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 2 Ed Sheeran -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7c3aed;font-weight:600;\">Live Music</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Ed Sheeran almost canceled the tour — then Philly saved the night</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://consequence.net/2026/09/ed-sheeran-considered-canceling-tour-macklemore/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/img2.jpg\" alt=\"Ed Sheeran\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">At Lincoln Financial Field on Saturday, Sheeran called the past week one of the worst of his life after Macklemore’s removal and a cascade of openers quitting. He said he considered scrapping the LOOP tour entirely — until ticket sales showed 50,000 fans still showing up. Closing speech: “Tonight has been honestly the best show of my life.”</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://consequence.net/2026/09/ed-sheeran-considered-canceling-tour-macklemore/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/fav_consequence.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Consequence&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 3 Chad Gilbert -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be185d;font-weight:600;\">Music</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">New Found Glory’s Chad Gilbert dies at 45</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.nme.com/news/music/new-found-glory-guitarist-chad-gilbert-dies-aged-45-3969796\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/img3.jpg\" alt=\"Chad Gilbert\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">The founding guitarist and co-songwriter behind early-2000s pop-punk staples like “My Friends Over You” died peacefully in his sleep this morning after a years-long fight with adrenal cancer, including emergency brain surgery earlier this year. His wife Lisa and bandmates remembered him as a husband and father first — and vowed his spirit will be on every stage they play.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.nme.com/news/music/new-found-glory-guitarist-chad-gilbert-dies-aged-45-3969796\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/fav_nme.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">NME&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 4 Jhene Aiko -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f766e;font-weight:600;\">Charts</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Jhené Aiko scores her first Billboard 200 No. 1 with <em>Westside Whimsy</em></h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/music/news/jhene-aiko-scores-first-no-1-albums-chart-westside-whimsy-1236870490/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/img4.jpg\" alt=\"Westside Whimsy album art\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Six years after <em>Chilombo</em>, Aiko’s fourth studio album bows at No. 1 with 74,000 equivalent units — the first R&amp;B album by a woman to top the chart this year, and the first since SZA’s <em>SOS</em>. Features from Kendrick Lamar, Tyga, and Larry June; it was also the only new top-10 debut this week.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/music/news/jhene-aiko-scores-first-no-1-albums-chart-westside-whimsy-1236870490/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3MG7Ev1JFfrwXKNCMxD5IK\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-20/images/fav_spotify.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Spotify&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- Bottom of the news -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#111;font-weight:700;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-top:22px;\">Bottom of the news</div>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:8px 18px 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#333;\">\n    <ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18px;\">\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Lucas Museum of Narrative Art opens to the public Tuesday in L.A. after a star-studded Saturday night gala co-chaired by Tom Cruise, Greta Gerwig, Spielberg, and more.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><em>Spider-Man: Brand New Day</em> adds ~$6.5M; domestic total ~$944.5M (all-time No. 1) and ~$2.45B worldwide.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><em>Practical Magic 2</em> slides ~60% to ~$12M in weekend two (~$49M domestic to date).</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Ella Langley’s “Choosin’ Texas” is on track tomorrow for the longest-running Hot 100 No. 1; her album <em>Dandelion</em> sits at No. 2 behind Aiko.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Madonna × Charli XCX “Danceteria Afterhours” still due Sept. 24 as Madonna heads into the VMAs with 11 nominations.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0;\">Next weekend: Brad Pitt’s <em>Heart of the Beast</em>, DreamWorks’ <em>Forgotten Island</em>, and A24’s <em>Primetime</em> with Robert Pattinson.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 36px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#888;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    Pop Culture Digest · Sunday, September 20, 2026<br>\n    Catch-up send · full-bleed mobile layout · from popculture@agentmail.to\n  </td></tr>\n\n</table>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n"}